          <description>The RX Individual Mask Registers are used to store the acceptance masks for ID filtering in Rx MBs and the Legacy Rx FIFO.
When the Legacy Rx FIFO is disabled (CAN_MCR.RFEN is negated), an individual mask is provided for each available Rx mailbox on a one-to-one correspondence. When the Legacy Rx FIFO is enabled (CAN_MCR.RFEN is asserted), an individual mask is provided for each Legacy Rx FIFO ID Filter Table Element on a one-to-one correspondence depending on the setting of $\newline$ CAN_CTRL2.RFFN (see \hyperref[legacy-rx-fifo]{"Legacy Rx FIFO"}).
CAN_RXIMR0 stores the individual mask associated with either MB0 or ID Filter Table Element 0, CAN_RXIMR1 stores the individual mask associated with either MB1 or ID Filter Table Element 1, and so on.
CAN_RXIMRn registers can only be accessed by the CPU when the FlexCAN is in Freeze mode; otherwise, they are blocked by hardware. The CAN_RXIMRn registers are not affected by reset. They are located in RAM and must be explicitly initialized prior to any reception.
The CAN_RXIMRn registers are not available if parameter IRMQ_EN is 0.</description>
          <addressOffset>0x8bc</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
           <fields>
            <field>
              <name>MI</name>
              <description>Each Individual Mask Bit masks the corresponding bit in both the mailbox filter and Legacy Rx FIFO ID Filter Table element in distinct ways. 
For mailbox filters, see the RXMGMASK register description.
For Legacy Rx FIFO ID Filter Table elements, see the RXFGMASK register description.
0b - The corresponding bit in the filter is ``don't care".
1b - The corresponding bit in the filter is checked.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>32</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>

