        <register>
        <name>CLKVLDDLY0</name>
          <description></description>
          <addressOffset>0x8c</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0x0000000f</resetValue>
           <fields>
            <field>
              <name>VAL</name>
              <description>Each CMU channel optinally support a detector which detecting over-time delay between monitored clock enable and monitored clock valid. 

CMU channel n starts counting the delay time when: 
 - CMU Channel n has monitored clock valid detector
 - And CTRL.EN[n]=1 
 - And CMU channel n's reference clock is enabled
 - And CMU channel n's monitored clock is enabled

The monitored clock valid need to come in time limitation configured by CLKVLDDLYn, or a clock-valid-miss event will initiate.
Refer to Chip-specific Information for maximum delay time of Monitored Clock Valid of each CMU channel.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>0</name>
                  <description>The clock valid needs to come in 1/16 of maximum delay time after clock enabled</description>
                  <value>0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>1</name>
